# Revision history for PAGI-ResponseBuilder

0.001000 - unreleased

  - PAGI::ResponseBuilder: collects a response's status, headers and cookies
    in stages and builds the body last, as an ordinary PAGI-Tools response
    value, for frameworks whose API sets those before the body.
  - A COOKBOOK section of fluent recipes (text, JSON with collected headers
    and cookies, HTML, redirect, no content, Problem, file, stream, another
    charset, replacing a body on error, a class of your own); a test runs
    each as published.
  - problem() for as('Problem', ...); headers() returns a copy of the header
    fields as a PAGI::Headers; text(), html() and json() take a trailing
    status, as PAGI::Response's did before 0.003000.
  - bytes() for a body of encoded bytes, sent as they are.
  - The SYNOPSIS is a complete small framework: hooks collect headers and
    cookies, a handler chooses each kind of body, an error handler replaces
    it, and the framework sends it; a test runs it as published.
